{{also|Cysteine|cystéine}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
An alteration of [[cystine]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
[[File:L-Cystein - L-Cysteine.svg|thumb|right|Skeletal formula of L-'''cysteine'''.]]
[[File:D-Cysteine.svg|thumb|right|Skeletal formula of D-'''cysteine'''.]]

# {{lb|en|amino acid}} A {{l|en|sulphur}}-[[containing]] [[nonessential amino acid]] C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>7</sub>NO<sub>2</sub>S found in most {{l|en|animal}} {{l|en|protein|proteins}}; it readily [[oxidize]]s to [[cystine]].

====Usage notes====
When used as the name of a substance, this noun is uncountable, but when used as the name of individual molecules, it is countable.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|E910}} when used as a [[food additive]]
* {{l|en|E920}} when used as an [[improving agent]]
* {{l|en|Cys}} when viewed as a monomer in proteins

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|homocysteine}}

